ult":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nSpring Boot 4 split every `spring-boot-starter-*` into an empty POM shell (no class files) plus a real, class-bearing module with the same name minus \"starter\" — confirmed by three sibling `index.json` files in this repo (`spring-boot-starter-couchbase`, `spring-boot-starter-couchbase-test`, `spring-boot-starter-data-couchbase`) that all say \"contains only META-INF, use `spring-boot-<x>:4.1.1` instead.\" The issue's artifact, `spring-boot-data-couchbase-test` (no \"starter\"), is exactly that real module — it's the one carrying the `@DataCouchbaseTest` test-slice annotation and its auto-configuration classes.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nKey findings from the worktree (no network access was available, so this is based on repo precedent + domain knowledge of Spring Boot's Couchbase test-slice design):\n\n- **No Couchbase Docker infrastructure exists yet** in `tests/tck-build-logic/.../allowed-docker-images/` (only sftp, mosquitto, greenmail, mariadb, microcks, mssql, mysql, nats, nginx, opengauss, postgres, rabbitmq, ryuk are pinned).\n- **Couchbase has no embedded/in-memory mode** (unlike `@DataJpaTest`'s default H2). Spring Boot's `CouchbaseAutoConfiguration`/`CouchbaseDataAutoConfiguration` eagerly open a real `Cluster`/`Bucket`, so a `@DataCouchbaseTest`-based context only loads successfully against a live server.\n- **This repo's own precedent confirms the pattern**: `tests/src/org.springframework.boot/spring-boot-testcontainers/4.1.1/build.gradle` adds an extra testcontainers module (`com.redis:testcontainers-redis:2.2.4`) beyond the scaffold defaults specifically to exercise a `@ServiceConnection`-backed container. The idiomatic, documented way to exercise `@DataCouchbaseTest` is the analogous `@Container CouchbaseContainer` + `@ServiceConnection` pattern, requiring the `org.testcontainers:couchbase` module and a `couchbase/server` image — neither of which the generated scaffold provides (it only adds the library jar + assertj-core).\n\nSince this satisfies \"concrete evidence that extra setup is needed,\" my decision is `advisory_preparation`.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"advisory_preparation\",\n  \"summary\": \"spring-boot-data-couchbase-test is the real (non-starter) module carrying @DataCouchbaseTest's auto-configuration; Couchbase has no embedded mode, so a meaningful context-loading test needs a live cluster, which the scaffold doesn't provide and no Couchbase Docker image is yet pinned in this repo.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"dependency\",\n      \"coordinate\": \"org.testcontainers:couchbase:1.20.4\",\n      \"scope\": \"testImplementation\",\n      \"reason\": \"Provides CouchbaseContainer for a @Container/@ServiceConnection-backed test, mirroring the pattern already used in tests/src/org.springframework.boot/spring-boot-testcontainers/4.1.1/build.gradle (com.redis:testcontainers-redis) for a comparable technology's service-connection test. Version is an estimate (no network access to verify against Maven Central) and should be confirmed by Gradle dependency resolution.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"docker_image\",\n      \"image\": \"couchbase/server:7.6.2\",\n      \"slug\": \"couchbase_server\",\n      \"reason\": \"No Couchbase image is currently pinned under allowed-docker-images/. A live cluster is required because CouchbaseAutoConfiguration/CouchbaseDataAutoConfiguration open a real Cluster/Bucket eagerly, with no embedded fallback. Tag/edition (Enterprise vs Community) is unverified due to lack of network access in this environment and must be confirmed by an actual Docker pull.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Prefer the idiomatic pattern demonstrated in tests/src/org.springframework.boot/spring-boot-testcontainers/4.1.1: declare the CouchbaseContainer as a @Bean annotated with @ServiceConnection inside a @TestConfiguration imported by the @DataCouchbaseTest class, letting Spring's TestcontainersLifecycleApplicationContextInitializer manage start/stop (no org.testcontainers:junit-jupiter dependency needed). Create at least one bucket via BucketDefinition and allow the query/index services to come up — call waitUntilReady() if available, since full cluster bootstrap (data+index+query+fts) is slow and may need a generous container startup timeout. Before committing to a real container, double check whether Testcontainers' CouchbaseContainer requires the Enterprise image tag (some versions depend on cluster-manager REST endpoints not present in Community edition) — Enterprise free-tier is normally fine for dev/test use, but confirm no production-licensing concern applies in CI.\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"Dependency version (org.testcontainers:couchbase) and Docker image tag/edition are best-effort estimates; this research environment had no network/Maven Central access to verify them, so local Gradle resolution and a real Docker pull are authoritative and may require adjusting the tag.\",\n    \"Couchbase server containers are heavier and slower to start than the other pinned images (postgres, mariadb, etc.), which may need a longer test timeout.\",\n    \"If local verification shows the real auto-configuration classes can be reached without a live cluster (e.g. by excluding CouchbaseAutoConfiguration and mocking the repository beans), this setup may turn out to be unnecessary — but that approach would miss coverage of the module's primary auto-configuration/import-selector classes, which is why the live-cluster path is recommended first.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":7238,"type":"result","duration_ms":434292,"uuid":"5f5d624e-c1ed-4fbb-9647-e731833ae0c0","ttft_stream_ms":1716,"time_to_request_ms":75,"first_content_frame_ms":1717,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

